WEBVTT

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.090
Chutaro! Chutaro!

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.690
It's time to go home!

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.130
Chutaro!

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.960
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.760
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.600
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.870
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.840
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.710
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.610
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.510
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.120
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.920
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot, we both</i>

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.020
<i>become stronger</i>

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.790
<i>and closer</i>

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.800
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.370
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.540
<i>Don't you know that good fortune 
comes to the gates of laughter?</i>

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.410
<i>Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:14.680
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:15.580
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.280
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.090
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.990
<i>We're pretty and cure cure</i>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.560
<i>Together we are</i>

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.630
<i>Pretty Cure...!</i>

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.770
Kiriya-kun!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.500
Honoka...?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.550
What is it, Grandmother?

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:22.040
I found some nice bamboo again this year.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.790
For the "Tanabata" Festival?

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.710
Do you want to help us 
decorate, too, Chutaro?

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.150
You have a cobweb on your head.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.490
Where were you anyway?

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:38.660
Chutaro's been acting 
strange since yesterday.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.480
He's been extremely restless...

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.090
He's been going back and forth in the yard.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.140
Really?

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.190
He has a really good appetite, too.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:53.340
Even after he had seconds, 
it didn't seem to be enough.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.690
"YOU'RE KIDDING! 
CHUTARO'S GOING TO BE A MOM?!"

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:28.140
You've done a great job of getting back 
the forth Prism Stone, little girls.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.620
Now we have six in our possession.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.590
There's only one left.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:33.900
Do you best.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.720
Why do you look so glum, little girls?

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.050
This one was a little 
rough on both of them...

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.400
That's why they can't really 
feel happy about it mepo.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.410
Why? What is it? Tell me all the details.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.830
They're not in the mood for that yet mipo.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.640
I think they want you 
to leave for today mepo.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.610
I see...

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.210
I'll be praying that you 
get the seventh Prism Stone

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.990
back as soon as possible, little girls.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.370
Come to think of it,

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:21.360
what happens to the Prism Stones 
that we put in the Hopish?

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.850
The Keeper takes them to a world

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.920
between the Field of Light 
and the Field of Rainbows,

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.930
in other words, an entirely different 
world, and guards them mepo.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.230
As long as they don't 
know where the Keeper is,

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.080
the stones are safe mipo.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.670
Is that right?

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:43.940
You sure have a big bamboo decoration 
for the "Tanabata" Festival.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.180
We live in a condo, so we can 
only decorate a small one.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.790
Ryota's always grumbling.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.330
What is it, Chutaro?

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.430
You want your food?

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.140
Chutaro's asking for his food.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.410
You're kidding! Not again?

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.500
Again?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.650
He's not eating it.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.810
Where is he bringing it anyway?

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.450
Chutaro gave birth to a puppy.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.930
But Chutaro's a male.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.560
That's right.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.420
Are you okay?

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.170
Here... Take him.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.880
He's so cute.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:53.080
Maybe he's Chutaro's kid.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.200
The mother dog couldn't raise 
him, so she brought him here.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.690
That can't be. This puppy has a collar...

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.170
He must be someone's pet.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:05.160
There's a name here.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.370
Moko...?

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:08.650
Maybe because he's always 
squirming (moko-moko).

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.560
So, you're Moko?

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.640
Okay... I won't do that again.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:19.810
Sasamori Apartments 5-203?

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:21.890
There's an address.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.550
That's not far from here.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.240
Let's take him home.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:33.660
Building 5... Building 5.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:36.530
Here it is.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.580
I wonder if they're out.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:48.540
There's no name.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.150
You're right.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.360
Maybe no one's living here.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.590
That can't be!

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.750
Let's ask someone.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:03.240
Next door? It looks like they moved out.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.020
I see...

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.750
We live in Building 3...

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.090
I don't recognize that dog either.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:19.700
It smells just like that place...

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.000
I wonder if it's Akio.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.220
Akio...?

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:31.650
I'm sure he's worried that you're gone.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:34.810
But...

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:44.070
I thought they were going to leave 
me alone in a strange place.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.670
And I didn't know what to do after that.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:50.980
I see...

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.680
There are so many people living here,

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.340
but they don't know too much 
about their neighbors, do they?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.260
That's true.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.760
It's Moko.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.760
Do you know Moko?

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:05.570
Akio moved to a house where they have 
a yard where he and Moko could play.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.520
Akio must be Moko's owner.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.470
Do you know where Akio's house is?

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:14.930
He told me to come and visit, 
but I don't really know.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.310
I see...

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:19.420
Akio's probably at the planetarium.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:22.710
He loves the planetarium, 
so he always goes there.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.780
Planetarium...?

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.040
Shall we go there?

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:29.370
Where did Chutaro and Moko go?

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:31.560
Chutaro!

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.320
Moko!

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.320
Chutaro!

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:38.990
Maybe Chutaro found a clue 
to find Moko's owners.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.150
You think so?

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.550
It continues down this way.

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:51.770
You can tell?

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.540
You're awesome, Chutaro.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:55.320
Show some respect when you address me.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.230
Chutaro-kun...

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.120
Hot off the grill...

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:13.670
Okay... okay...

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.800
We don't have time for that now!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.430
I almost had it.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.000
The smell is gone.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.770
What are we going to do, Chutaro-kun?

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:37.410
Let's just go in this direction.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.360
Wait, Chutaro-kun!

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:40.810
Really?

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:45.670
The big dog picked up the little one, 
and they went toward the station.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.300
Chutaro and Moko...

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.790
That looks so delicious.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.720
You eat like a horse, Nagisa!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.580
My "yakitori" (grilled chicken on a skewer).

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:04.020
Nagisa...?

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:04.790
What?

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:08.270
It's the planetarium.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.680
Moko's owner, Akio loved 
this place, didn't he?

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:18.220
Maybe we can find some kind of clue here...

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:20.690
But even if we find the owner,

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.520
it won't do any good if we don't have Moko...

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.600
Moko will be fine. Chutaro is with him...

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:28.490
If he can't find the owner, 
he'll come back home.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.290
That's true.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.680
Shall we check it out then?

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.040
This brings back memories.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.030
I haven't been here since 
I was in grade school.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:10.190
People who came here wrote their wishes here.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:12.890
Maybe Akio wrote one, too.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:15.000
Let's try and find it.

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:26.580
What's wrong, Moko? Are you tired?

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:30.030
I won't see Akio again.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.060
We've tried so hard, and 
we couldn't find him.

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:33.530
Moko...?

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:37.020
If we can't find Akio's house,

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.500
will you be my big brother, Chutaro-kun?

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.780
Please!

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.680
We'll find him.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:47.910
I'm sure we'll find him.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:49.610
Really?

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:51.080
I'm sure.

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:56.820
"I wish I could be a baker." That's so cute.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.120
When I was little, I wanted 
to be a Battle Ranger.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:02.950
Sounds so like you, Nagisa.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:04.590
I wanted to be a florist.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:06.560
Not a scientist?

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:10.220
I was still little at the time.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:11.540
Look at this one...

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.830
"I wish Papa wouldn't pass 
gas in front of people."

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:20.600
It's been a while... Let's 
go inside the planetarium.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:24.210
But we came to find a clue to where Akio is.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.080
We don't have time to do things like that.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.530
If we look at the stars, and clear our heads,

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:31.040
I'm sure we'll get a good 
idea where to find a clue.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.820
Let's get a ticket.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.040
Nagisa...!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:41.000
"I wish Moko would come home."

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:46.240
This smell...?

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.870
What is it, Chutaro-kun?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:54.590
There aren't any people in here... 
I wonder if we're a little early.

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:56.130
It's okay... It's nice and quiet.

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:58.860
When you were in grade school,

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:01.280
didn't you hear the story of "Tanabata" here?

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.670
I did.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:06.520
On July 7th, Hikoboshi 
(the Cow Herder Star) would make a bridge

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.840
with some kind of birds at 
"Amanogawa" (the Milky Way),

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.320
so he can meet Orihime (Weaving Princess).

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.000
The birds are magpies.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.320
Why do I smell those two 
in a place like this?

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.670
What's wrong, Chutaro-kun?

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.120
Wait for me!

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:31.340
When they room darkens,

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:34.040
it's like the ceiling 
opens up, and it's like...

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:38.020
The night skies filled with shining stars...

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:47.730
I feel a really sinister 
presence nearby mepo!

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:50.350
I feel it really close by mipo!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.190
It's beautiful!

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.840
Zakenna!

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.870
The sinister presence...?

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:15.840
Don't tell me, it's...?

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:16.670
This is it mipo!

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:18.390
Hurry, and transform mepo!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:21.480
Zakenna!

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.540
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.390
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.140
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.010
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:07.410
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.850
Go back to where you came from!

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.750
Zakenna!

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:16.500
Zakenna...

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.230
Zakenna!

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:39.950
Chutaro!

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:48.090
Zakenna!

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.790
Za... Za... zakenna!

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:05.210
They move out of the body 
just when we have them...

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:08.340
At this rate, it could go on forever.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:12.500
That's it! Over there!

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:15.440
Black Thunder!

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:17.810
White Thunder!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:28.190
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.060
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:35.570
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:42.770
Gomenna! Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.650
Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.670
It's over, isn't it?

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.140
It's still here mipo!

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:51.050
There's still a really 
awesome presence here mepo!

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:55.730
That was pretty good.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:57.920
It's him!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:02.230
Today, I'll get you to tell me the 
whereabouts of the Prism Stones.

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:03.990
You must be kidding!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:05.190
Why would we tell you...?

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:14.340
What's wrong? Are you so 
scared, you can't move?

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:15.830
What?

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:22.780
There's no use resisting.

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:24.260
He's strong.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:27.700
He's totally different from 
all the others, after all.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.800
Tell me... Where are the Prism Stones?

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:41.260
Do you want me to hurt you again?

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:47.100
I see... In that case... I'll do as you wish.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:50.200
It's impossible! There's 
no way you'll find them.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:53.680
That's right. They're in a 
place even we can't get to.

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.640
A place where you can't get to?

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:58.200
That's right mepo.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.900
The Stone Keeper is guarding 
them, so they're safe.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.130
The Stone Keeper?

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:09.050
Do you mean Wisdom?

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:12.020
How did he know the name of the Keeper mepo?

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:14.990
I see... So Wisdom has the stones...?

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:19.320
In that case, I need to prepare things first.

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:21.680
I'll be back.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.870
He knew the name of the Stone Keeper.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.320
We didn't even know it.

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:46.820
Don't tell me...?

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:48.580
No, it couldn't be!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.620
I'm really, really nervous mipo!

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:53.430
Is that your master, Chutaro-kun?

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:55.200
How awesome.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:58.010
More like a close friend than a master.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.850
I knew she was doing something secretly,

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:02.610
but I had no idea that this is what it was.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:05.330
Chutaro!

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:07.670
So you were safe...

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:11.870
What's that?

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:15.710
"I wish that Chiko will come home..."

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:17.120
It's Moko not Chiko...

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:19.700
Isn't this a picture of Moko and Akio?

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.660
There's an address written here, too.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:25.830
Good work, Chutaro!

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:36.090
It's Moko! Moko came home!

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:40.630
Moko... Moko!

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.020
Where were you? I missed you!

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:49.240
Thank you! Come back with 
Chutaro, and visit again.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.080
We'll see you again!

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:53.900
Bye-bye, Chutaro-kun!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:56.000
Bye-bye, Moko.

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:05.350
You really impressed me this time, Chutaro.

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:07.010
Good boy!

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:10.650
Aren't you lonely now that Moko is gone?

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:20.300
I'm worried about that guy 
from the Dotsuku Zone.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.260
We can't let our guard down.

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:25.140
You're really worried about 
something else, aren't you?

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:31.130
But we'll just have to do our best.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:35.390
For Kiriya-kun who gave us his Prism Stone...

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:37.210
We do, don't we?

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:08.300
That night, Honoka cried...

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:11.340
She cried until there 
were no more tears left.

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:16.580
Honoka... Hang in there.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:25.180
<i>Ah- Let's go!</i>

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:29.120
<i>Get you! L-O-V-E Love Love!</i>

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:29.880
<i>Get you!</i>

00:22:29.430 --> 00:22:32.460
<i>I can't do this! I'd rather be a</i>

00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:35.500
<i>young lady than a fighter and</i>

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:38.040
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:42.070
<i>And melt your body and soul into sweets</i>

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:47.850
<i>like chocolate parfait or handsome men</i>

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:52.180
<i>I'm at the age to seriously 
fall head over heels in love</i>

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:55.250
<i>I wanted to confess my love again today</i>

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:59.760
<i>For the sake of the earth 
For the sake of everyone</i>

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:06.260
<i>That's good, too, but haven't 
you forgotten something?</i>

00:23:07.370 --> 00:23:13.870
<i>I'm a teenager with a heart 
throbbing exciting dream</i>

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:20.380
<i>I don't want to lose that 
normal everyday routine</i>

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:23.110
<i>I just can't do this! 
It's romance rather than</i>

00:23:23.110 --> 00:23:26.350
<i>stress, isn't it?</i>

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:28.520
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode.</i>

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:32.120
<i>Isn't that the best source of power?</i>

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:35.330
<i>I just can't do this! I'd rather cuddle</i>

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:38.130
<i>than fight and...</i>

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:40.370
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:40.370 --> 00:23:43.030
<i>That's the most peaceful way</i>

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:49.610
<i>So why am I stuffing my face 
with chocolates like this?</i>

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:54.680
We're going on a training camp...

00:23:54.680 --> 00:23:56.180
For special lacrosse training.

00:23:56.180 --> 00:23:56.890
What a coincidence!

00:23:56.890 --> 00:23:58.290
I have a training camp for 
the science club, too.

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:00.200
The hot summer mountain, 
working up a good sweat

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:02.220
and the refreshing breeze. And curry...

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:02.930
Curry?

00:24:02.930 --> 00:24:05.170
And look at the beautiful autumn colors...

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:08.350
Autumn colors...? But it's summer!

00:24:08.860 --> 00:24:10.550
What is this peculiar feeling?

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:11.720
It's the guy from other day...

00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:12.550
Not him?

00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:16.400
"DANGER! 
THE SUMMER TRAINING CAMP NIGHTMARE"

00:24:16.580 --> 00:24:18.060
Oh no! The Hopish...

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:19.640
Did he take them?
